---
import ResearchFigureFrame from './ResearchFigureFrame.astro';
---

<ResearchFigureFrame
  className="interaction-path-figure"
  figureNumber="01"
  title="Same intent, different interface path"
  caption="Conversation can also trigger an action directly. The handoff only applies if its result remains outside the table. Neither path is inherently faster, more capable, or more accurate."
>
  <div class="paths">
    <section aria-labelledby="conversation-path-title">
      <h4 id="conversation-path-title">Conversation-mediated</h4>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="step">01</span><span>Describe the desired state in prose</span></li>
        <li><span class="step">02</span><span>Conversational interpretation</span></li>
        <li><span class="step">03</span><span>Action or result</span></li>
        <li class="conditional"><span class="step">IF</span><span>When the result lives outside the table, the user carries it back</span></li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="embedded-path-title">
      <h4 id="embedded-path-title">Embedded capability</h4>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="step">01</span><span>Act inside the table</span></li>
        <li><span class="step">02</span><span>Capability receives a narrow job</span></li>
        <li><span class="step">03</span><span>Table updates in place</span></li>
      </ol>
    </section>
  </div>
  <div class="shared-result">
    <span>Shared end state</span>
    <p>The table reflects the requested state if either path is integrated to reach it.</p>
  </div>
</ResearchFigureFrame>

<style>
  .interaction-path-figure :global(p), .interaction-path-figure :global(h4),
  .interaction-path-figure :global(ol), .interaction-path-figure :global(li) { margin: 0; }
  .interaction-path-figure :global(ol) { padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .paths { display: grid; gap: 1.75rem; }
  .paths section { min-width: 0; }
  .paths section + section { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-top: 1.5rem; }
  h4 { color: var(--text-primary); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 0.9375rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.45; }
  .paths ol { margin-top: 1rem !important; }
  .paths li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2.25rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0.75rem; padding: 0.55rem 0; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .paths li + li { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); }
  .step { color: var(--accent); font-family: var(--font-mono-ui); font-size: 0.6875rem; line-height: 2; }
  .conditional { color: var(--text-secondary) !important; }
  .conditional .step { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .shared-result { display: grid; gap: 0.35rem 1.5rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong); padding-top: 1rem; }
  .shared-result span { color: var(--accent); font-family: var(--font-mono-ui); font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .shared-result p { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .paths { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0; }
    .paths section:first-child { padding-right: 1.5rem; }
    .paths section + section { border-top: 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 0 0 0 1.5rem; }
    .shared-result { grid-template-columns: 10rem minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }
</style>

<style>
  :global(.research-reading .research-prose figure.interaction-path-figure) { border-radius: 0 !important; }
  :global(.research-reading .research-prose figure.interaction-path-figure) .shared-result p { font-size: 0.875rem !important; line-height: 1.6 !important; }
</style>
